<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who the Modern Series is for</h2>
        <p>The Modern Series is for people who want a clean, contemporary look and flexibility on where the spa goes. Models range from the 2-person Bella MS, only 34.5 inches wide and narrow enough to fit through most standard doorways, to the 6-person Encore MS and Jubilee MS. The Retreat MS is a best-seller thanks to its compact footprint and deep bucket seats.</p>
        <h2>Electrical: start on 110V, upgrade later</h2>
        <p>Nordic lists Modern Series models as <strong>110V/220V convertible</strong>: about a 1 kW heater on 110V or a 4 kW heater on 220V. That means you can plug in and start soaking without a new circuit, then add a 240V circuit later if you want much faster heating. It's a good middle ground for condos, townhomes and tight backyards. Our <a href="/guides/110v-vs-240v-hot-tubs/">110V vs 240V guide</a> shows how much faster a 4 kW heater recovers.</p>
        <h2>Indoors, outdoors, and Utah winters</h2>
        <p>The compact Bella MS opens up indoor, sunroom and basement-walkout placements that larger spas can't reach. Indoor spas need ventilation and moisture planning. For outdoor use through a Utah winter, consider the Nordic Wrap insulation upgrade, keep a tight cover on, and if you run on 110V, keep the lid closed between soaks. See our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">winter guide</a>.</p>
        <h2>See the Modern Series in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

